From: sdm845-mainline <https://gitlab.com/sdm845-mainline/linux>
Subject: sdm845-mainline device support, rebased on v7.1.6

Squashed device delta of the sdm845-mainline tree (branch sdm845/7.1-dev,
head 85f1df2a4ec7 "sdm845.config: further cleanup and some moved into
misc.config", 2026-05-08) on top of the mainline stable tag v7.1.6.

Previously this package consumed the fork's own tarball (sdm845-7.1-rc1-r0),
which pins 7.1.0-rc1; the fork has not been rebased since May 2026 and 7.1-rc1
is an -rc. This patch keeps exactly the fork's device content (SDM845 DTS,
panels/touchscreens, camera, qdsp6 audio, IPA/power bits) while the base moves
to the current 7.1.y stable, so the kernel picks up ~6 stable releases of fixes
(including USB-audio fixes and "arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium:
Correct IPA FW path").

Generated with:
  git merge v7.1.6            # into sdm845/7.1-dev
  git diff v7.1.6..HEAD

Merge conflicts (8) resolved as:
  - Makefile, drivers/char/tpm/tpm_crb.c, fs/nfs/write.c, io_uring/tctx.c,
    net/sunrpc/xprtrdma/{rpc_rdma,transport}.c -> take v7.1.6.
    The fork branched pre-rc1 (merge base ff9726d7a006) so its copies of these
    files are stale snapshots of subsystem trees Linus merged differently;
    none carry device changes.
  - arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi (framebuffer node
    name) and sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c (commented-out state
    assignment) -> keep the fork's version.

